        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Aloe affinis is a species of flowering plant in the Asphodelaceae family. It is endemic to Limpopo, Gauteng, and Mpumalanga, of South Africa. It grows {{Convert abbreviated|200-300|mm}} tall excluding inflorescence, with 16–20 leaves per plant, each leaf being roughly 200 mm long x 50–100 mm wide."
